{
  /*
   * L0 storage — the port, the store catalogue, the migration table, and the
   * two implementations that need no platform.
   *
   * WHAT CHANGED WHEN THIS MOVED, AND WHY THE LIB SHRANK
   *
   * In web this project carried `"lib": ["ES2023", "DOM"]`, because
   * `idb-driver.ts` lived here and IndexedDB, BroadcastChannel and the quota
   * estimate were its job. Those files did not come along: every DOM-shaped
   * storage file stayed in `web/src/kg/storage`, which is where the platform
   * adapters belong and where `check-platform.mjs` always intended the line to
   * fall. What is left is DOM-free — measured, not assumed: compiling this
   * directory under `"lib": ["ES2023"]` with `"types": []` produced exactly
   * three errors, all of them `TextEncoder`/`TextDecoder`, and no DOM name at
   * all.
   *
   * So the lib is now ES2023 like everything else in the package, and the
   * DOM-versus-no-DOM reason for keeping storage in its own project is gone.
   * Two reasons to keep the project anyway:
   *
   * 1. `types/text-codec.d.ts` below, which is scoped to this directory and
   *    nowhere else. Folded into the core project it would grant `TextEncoder`
   *    to `core`, `repo` and `tools`, which is a capability none of them has any
   *    business having on Hermes.
   * 2. `composite` + `disableSourceOfProjectReferenceRedirect` in the consuming
   *    projects means `repo` type-checks against this layer's EMITTED .d.ts
   *    rather than against its source. That is the layer boundary restated as a
   *    build artifact, and it survives the next driver that does need a platform.
   *
   * Declarations only, into node_modules/.tmp. Nothing is bundled from here —
   * both apps compile the sources themselves — so this emit is type-checking
   * scaffolding and belongs beside the .tsbuildinfo.
   *
   * `rootDir` is the package root rather than `kg/storage`, because a composite
   * project rejects an input file outside its rootDir and the two .d.ts inputs
   * live in `types/`. Nothing reads the emitted layout, so its shape does not
   * matter.
   */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.storage.tsbuildinfo",
    "lib": ["ES2023"],
    "types": [],

    "composite": true,
    "declaration": true,
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true,
    "noEmit": false,
    "rootDir": ".",
    "outDir": "./node_modules/.tmp/storage"
  },
  "include": ["kg/storage", "types/portable-globals.d.ts", "types/text-codec.d.ts"]
}
